From 201961bbeb4e8ffe0d962a00ac751b9293c4c027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Price <jrprice@google.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:23:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [metal] Enable full polyfill for extractBits

This avoids a driver bug that incorrectly treats offset=32, count=0 as
undefined behavior.

Fixed: 587021111
Change-Id: Ie5d07afc00278eb91235bea0c86223cbf357521f
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/360955
Commit-Queue: James Price <jrprice@google.com>
Commit-Queue: David Neto <dneto@google.com>
Reviewed-by: David Neto <dneto@google.com>

(cherry picked from commit ce281c466b2257a504122cbb7e202d5e1a8b780f)

FlyWeb (siguiente-3): ported to the Dawn of M156 (branch point
0a2c7df818 of chromium/8078) from main, as M159 did in e6ee1e5319
(bugs 588740235, 587021111). Context-only adaptation: the new toggle
goes at the end of the M156 lists in Toggles.cpp and Toggles.h; the
other hunks apply with offsets.
